 "notes": "N097. ImageStream sandbox (S-BIAD452: brightfield/side-scatter images, 9 markers measured on EVERY cell, 3 donors, each held out once; N080 ResNet-50 models). Types = hierarchical gates on the held-out donor's own measured labels (evaluation only). a-c lymphocytes of held-out donor 0: measured CD3 vs CD19 (T and B cells form two separate clouds) vs predictions of the all-marker and one-marker models (one continuous anti-diagonal band). d r(CD3, CD19) within lymphocytes, rings = 3 donors: measured -.63/-.88/-.68; predictions are MORE anticorrelated (-.84..-.93): the models encode a single lymphocyte axis with CD3 and CD19 at opposite ends. e but where a cell sits on that axis tracks its true lineage only partly: AUROC B vs T .74/.94/.46 (all-marker) and .81/.90/.51 (one-marker); on donor 2 predicted CD19 has r .09 with the measured CD19, so B vs T is at chance. f Pearson r of predicted vs measured CD3 and CD19 over all held-out cells (rings = donors; paired t, Holm). g-i mean z of every marker per gated type: measured vs predicted; predictions reproduce the granulocyte/monocyte/lymphocyte split but compress the lymphocyte subtypes (T4/T8/B/NK) toward each other. Paired t vs measured (d) / all-marker (e), Holm (3 donors: low power). Corr-loss arms (N096) are added when present.",
